        "original_id": "dc6e40c5-b260-5924-9969-c3f23b9e34ca",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- People: Rihanna, Cobb\n- Songs: \"SOS\", \"Tainted Love\"\n- Albums: A Girl Like Me\n- Works: Rihanna videography\n- Topics: music videos, video albums, television programs, films, television commercials, dance-pop, sampling\n\nFacts:\n- In 1965, Cobb wrote the song \"Tainted Love.\"\n- In 1981, Soft Cell recorded \"Tainted Love.\"\n- In 2006, Rihanna released her second studio album A Girl Like Me.\n- In 2006, \"SOS\" was released as the lead single from Rihanna's album A Girl Like Me.\n- \"SOS\" is a song by Barbadian singer Rihanna.\n- \"SOS\" is a dance-pop song that samples Soft Cell's 1981 recording of \"Tainted Love.\"\n- Three separate videos were released for Rihanna's song \"SOS,\" and all of them contained various dance sequences.\n- Rihanna has released four video albums and has appeared in fifty-two music videos, six films, ten television programs, and eight television commercials.",
